Data for "enchantment install init openrc" (enchant_install_init and
enchant_install_init_settings_openrc in lib/lib.install):

  depends    answers for sorcery, "spell:dependency:on|off" (see systemd/)
  presets/   openrc.p answers "SysVinit compatibility" with yes: without it
             OpenRC installs no /sbin/init (openrc-init), halt, reboot, ...
             and no getties
  replaces   spells dispelled before openrc is cast (and restored if it
             fails): simpleinit-msb (owns /sbin/init, ...) and init.d
             (conflicts with openrc, which provides INITSCRIPTS)
  providers  "spell PROVIDER" rewritten to openrc in sorcery's records
  recast     installed spells to recompile: procps-ng builds pidof only
             without simpleinit-msb, which shipped it
  check      spells that must be installed afterwards
  init.d/    service scripts SMGL's spells don't ship: udev, udev-trigger,
             udev-settle (eudev), metalog, nscd, sshd, dhcpcd,
             wpa_supplicant (Gentoo's, adapted; see the headers), and
             networking (ifup -a for /etc/network/interfaces, our own)
  conf.d/    their settings (copied only where none exist)
  local.d/   runs /etc/sysconfig/bootmisc and haltmisc, like simpleinit's
             smgl-misc
  runlevels  "service runlevel [file]": enabled when the file exists in the
             target (sshd too if it was enabled under simpleinit)
